\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Which structures survive refinement}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{Stokes and #{\covwedge^2=0} commute with dyadic subdivision, by
\ref{fdip-00OX}. On each finite calculus, #{\extD^2=-\covsq} holds
for the counting weights of \ref{fdip-00OL} and for the positive
weights of \ref{fdip-00OP}. Those weights are declared on that
calculus.}

\p{Three structures fail. The cup product of \ref{fdip-0093}
and the unweighted adjoint fail on the cochains of
\ref{fdip-00OZ}. The massive Laplacian fails because the
retained shape of \ref{fdip-00P0} is #{T_q(t)} when #{t\neq 1}.
The massless Dirichlet form matches only after the declared
factor of two, and only on the affine extensions named there.}
